                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "2\\pi a+2\\sqrt{c^2-(a-b)^2}-2(a-b)\\cos^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{a-b}{c}\\right)",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p40-q16-d-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Each tangent has length ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\sqrt{c^2-(a-b)^2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; add both tangents and the exterior arcs. The inverse cosine is in radians.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Using the same angle $\\theta$ and straight tangent length $d$ as in (a),\n$$\\begin{align*}d^2&=c^2-(a-b)^2\\\\d&=\\sqrt{c^2-(a-b)^2},\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{a-b}{c}\\\\\\theta&=\\cos^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{a-b}{c}\\right).\\end{align*}$$\nAdding the two exterior arcs and two tangent segments gives\n$$\\begin{align*}L&=a(2\\pi-2\\theta)+2b\\theta+2d\\\\L&=2\\pi a+2\\sqrt{c^2-(a-b)^2}-2(a-b)\\cos^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{a-b}{c}\\right).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 57
